---
import Resumen from "../../layouts/Resumen.astro";

export const prerender = true;

/**
 * What a subscriber sees after "delete everything".
 *
 * Prerendered and identityless, and both follow from what just happened: there is no row left
 * to read, no token that still names anything, and nothing to personalise with. That is the
 * page working correctly rather than a limitation — a confirmation that could still greet
 * somebody by name would be evidence the button had not done what it said.
 *
 * ## It states the subprocessor tail rather than claiming a clean sweep
 *
 * ADR 0010: "'Delete everything' is scoped honestly, because a subprocessor tail exists that
 * we cannot clear. Resend retains email and log data for 30 days on every plan below
 * Enterprise, keeps backups for 7 days, and maintains its own automatic suppression list
 * holding addresses in *plaintext*."
 *
 * Saying so here, and not only in the privacy notice, is the difference between a promise and
 * a claim. This is the one moment somebody is actually reading about their own deletion, and
 * the sentence they would most resent finding out later is the one about copies we do not
 * control.
 */
---

<Resumen title="Borrado" heading="Listo, ya no tenemos nada tuyo">
  <p data-testid="erased">
    Borramos tu correo y tus búsquedas. No te queda nada en Pawster y no te vamos a escribir
    más.
  </p>

  <p data-testid="subprocessor-tail">
    <!--
      The honest scope. Claiming this reached every copy everywhere would be false, and a
      reader who found out later would be right to disbelieve the rest of the page.
    -->
    Lo único que puede quedar por unos días son las copias que guarda Resend, la empresa que
    manda nuestros correos: los mensajes y sus registros se les borran solos a los 30 días, y
    sus copias de seguridad a los 7. Eso no lo controlamos nosotros.
  </p>

  <p data-testid="dnc-note">
    <!--
      Only true for somebody who reported us as spam, and phrased so it is not a lie for
      everybody else: the page cannot tell which reader this is, because the row it would have
      had to read is the one that was just destroyed.
    -->
    Si alguna vez marcaste nuestro correo como spam, guardamos un código del que no se puede
    sacar tu dirección, y nada más. Es lo que hace que el formulario se niegue a inscribirte
    otra vez, que es justo lo que pediste al marcarlo.
  </p>

  <p>
    Si algún día quieres volver, puedes <a href="/resumen">guardar una búsqueda nueva</a>
    desde cero.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/privacidad">Qué guardamos y por cuánto tiempo</a></p>
</Resumen>
